\f0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::2><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f3\i\fs26 Who was this loon?
\f1\i0  Sarah wondered. No time at all elapsed before she identified the celebrity host of 
\f3\i Random Camera
\f1\i0 . In a fit of raging disgust, she put the day\'92s supply of vibrators among the muffins. The teddy bears and bunny rabbits quaked with fright. She cursed Alexander\'92s name. There was only one man who rescued her from the bombing: Mr Fairy Boxers.\
\
Sarah required none of the advanced medicines and procedures available to her. Astonishingly, she recovered from her injuries within two days. Rather than investigate her remarkable abilities, doctors, nurses, bathroom orderlies and professorial boffins took them as further evidence of the genetic superiority of the Airborne, and were heard wondering aloud if eugenics hadn\'92t been retired rather too early.\
Cracker regained consciousness, significantly ignored and untreated, in a sweaty bed in a maze of bacterially alarming smudges. The colours of everything Cracker saw were too organically decaying for description; the greys were too green and yellow, the greens and yellows were too brown, and the browns were too much like the vomit he coughed up when he registered how much his skull hurt. The nurses gave him dusty pills the diameter of party pies and told him to rest.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
