\pard\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\fi360\sl264\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs26 Suffering too much from pollen, Sarah checked herself out early. She felt fully recovered anyway, and was anxious to thank Cracker.\
When she climbed the fire-escape stairs and entered the ward, she almost gagged with the stench. However, she was determined to press on.\
\'93Can I help you?\'94 the orderly at the ward desk asked.\
\'93I doubt it.\'94 Sarah strode past with her authoritative gait, between the rows of paint-chipped frames aching at holding saggy mattresses complaining of saggy patients. She almost passed Cracker without recognition.\
\'93Sarah!\'94 he called out.\
She gasped when he held her gaze with his unblinking right eye. His blackened left eye was bruised shut, and seeped a dilute blood-ooze that trickled over the lumps, cuts, scratches, burns and bruises that contrived to construct something not too dissimilar to a face.\
\'93Oh, my tax accountants! What are they doing to you?\'94 She fled to his side and grasped his hand.\
\'93Ow!\'94\
She released his hand. \'93Are they even treating you?\'94\
\'93The doctors diagnosed it as acute sunburn.\'94\
\'93What? But \'85 the cuts and bruises \'85 you eyebrows and most of your hair is singed off.\'94\
\'93Shaving accident.\'94\
\'93This is appalling!\'94 she sputtered. \'93I\'92ve never seen such \'85 
\f3\i squalor
\f1\i0  \'85\'94 
\f3\i Only a quick hover-copt jump from where I live
\f1\i0 , she thought, but could not bring herself to admit it.\
\'93You\'92ve never seen Cloudborne health care before then. All they prescribe is sticking plaster and suppositories.\'94 Cracker was about to remark that he had a better medical kit at home, but thought wiser of making such facts known in public spaces.\
Sarah made her spine straight with decision making. \'93You\'92re coming with me,\'94 she said. \'93He\'92s coming with me,\'94 she announced to the ward.\
\'93You can do better, dearie,\'94 said a withered nurse stumbling by on a cane.\
\'93Thank you, that would be most kind,\'94 Cracker said to Sarah.\
\'93I need a wheelchair,\'94 Sarah demanded.\
The withered nurse cackled.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
