\pard\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\fi360\sl264\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs26 Sarah returned a half-hour later, having purloined (temporarily) a wheelchair from an Airborne hospital. Cracker constructed himself into it with admirable resolve and tenacity. Sarah wheeled him to the stairwell, where they met two orderlies she paid to carry Cracker in wheelchair to the ground floor. From there, she pushed and shoved across unreliable ground to the nearest hover-pad stalk, where she and Cracker made their escape.\
They made most of the journey to Cracker\'92s apartment discreetly by Cloudborne groundcab, which served to enhance Sarah\'92s experience and understanding of the deteriorating Cloudborne lifestyle. Everything she saw was worn-down, broken, taped, jury-rigged, bent to shape, chipped, corroded, smeared, or tied up with string. \'93These are are a few of my ghastliest things,\'94 Sarah sang under her breath. The seats of the groundcab were torn and exploded springs. The doors to the back seat were clearly from another model of vehicle entirely, and didn\'92t shut properly. Gaps between the doors and wheel arches allowed Sarah to see through to the street. The steering wheel was almost completely missing. The driver steered by grasping the stubs of the steering wheel spokes. She braked by stomping on the floor like she was exterminating cockroaches. She accelerated by rocking back and forward in her seat, as if that would quicken the tired vehicle\'92s pace.\
When they reached Cracker\'92s front door, he presented his armpit, but his door stayed resolutely shut.\
\'93It didn\'92t even read me,\'94 he complained.\
\'93You might have to stand up,\'94 Sarah said. She helped him to his feet and supported him while he lifted his arm again. The door clicked open, and Cracker slumped into the wheelchair.\
\'93Not exactly disability-friendly,\'94 Cracker said solemnly.\
\'93No,\'94 Sarah agreed.\
Sarah was dismayed by the size and condition of Cracker\'92s living space, but did her best to hide it. Cracker wheeled himself to his room, bundled onto the bed, and passed out.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
